ety of  staff  residents and families in may mcdermott  lost her mother  by then she says there was little of  elsie left  she said this isn't living maureen this  is only  existing in her mother's memory a vow to  keep fighting  it started with this meeting with  ontario's new minister of long-term care  who has promised to build 30 000 new  beds in the next decade  and update legislation to enhance  accountability measures  i don't envy him or anybody stepping  into the role in the mess  that was left by the previous minister  but i'm i'm hopeful  change she says would be elsie's legacy  karen lieberman global news  toronto  winning women up next the athletes  adding to canada's olympic glory at the  tokyo games  in a stunning move the star of the u.s  women's gymnastics squad pulled out of  the artistic team final today simone  biles says  she needs to focus on her mental health  the 24 year old withdrew after just  one rotation she says a shaky vault made  her realize she wasn't  in the right headspace bile says she  didn't want to jeopardize her health and  well-being or risk a medal for her team  the rest of her team did go on to win  silver  the team representing the russian  olympic committee took gold it's unclear  if biles will compete in her five  other events which include defending her  all-round title  on thursday japanese tennis star naomi  osaka was knocked out of the women's  tournament today and a huge upset  osaka who was ranked second lost in the  third round  the olympic tournament was her first  major competition in nearly two months  after she sat out both the french open  and wimbledon  to focus on her mental health japan is  still leading the way  in gold medals here's a look at where  things stand japan has 10  goals now the us and china each have  nine  canada has two and is ranked eighth  overall  one of those golds was won today in  weight lifting it capped off  a four medal day for canadian athletes  this country also won its first ever